# Build context filter for Dockerfile.api (context = repository root).
# Keeping the context small makes `docker build` fast and keeps secrets and
# developer junk out of the image entirely.

# Secrets — env values are injected at RUN time (compose env_file), never baked
# into a layer. A baked .env would be readable by anyone who pulls the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.agents
.superpowers
.codex_tmp

# Frontend: a separate image with its own Dockerfile and context. Only the
# heavy derived directories are listed (not frontend/ itself) so a frontend
# build that uses the repository root as its context still works.
**/node_modules
.npm-cache
frontend/dist
frontend/.angular
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
.playwright-cli

# Python caches, local virtualenvs and pip scratch dirs.
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, a .dockerignore pattern is matched against the WHOLE
# relative path, so `__pycache__/` alone would only exclude a top-level one —
# the nested caches inside api/ and scraper/ need the `**/` prefix.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
env
*.egg-info
pip-build-tracker-*
pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*
pip-install-*

# Tests are deliberately NOT shipped: the runtime image should contain only
# what production executes. api/tests/ adds fixtures, fakes and scripted
# engines that have no business inside a production container, and CI runs the
# suite against the repository checkout rather than against the image.
api/tests
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache
.pytest-cache
.pytest-tmp
.pytest-*
pytest-cache-files-*

# Generated data, logs and local artifacts
output/
outputs/
logs/
tmp/
**/*.log
*.csv
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
migration_preview.sql

# Docs, editor and OS files — nothing in the image reads them
docs/
**/*.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Container definitions themselves
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
